  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/util.cc",
    "description": "In ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(const MonthDayNanoIntervalType&), the code iterates using data_->length and reads MonthDayNanos elements from data_->buffers[1] without validating that buffer[1] is large enough for length * sizeof(MonthDayNanos). For malformed IPC dictionary data, length can exceed the actual values buffer size, causing out-of-bounds read (global-buffer-overflow) at `tmp = data[i]` (util.cc:210) during endian swap.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzed IPC stream provides a dictionary batch that is accepted by reader.cc::ReadDictionary, then context.swap_endian is true (non-native endian schema with ensure_native_endian enabled), so reader calls internal::SwapEndianArrayData on decoded ArrayData. If the dictionary value type is MonthDayNanoInterval and metadata sets a large array length relative to the provided values buffer, ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(MonthDayNanoIntervalType) trusts length and OOB-reads buffer[1]."
  },
